## 4. Automated Tooling to Support This Audit

- [ ] Run a repository-wide grep for common hardcoded-value smells: currency symbols (`Rs\.`, `PKR`, `\$`), hardcoded percentage tax patterns (`0\.1[0-9]`, `\* 0\.17`), suspicious literal arrays of objects with `name`/`price`/`sku`-like keys outside of seed/test/fixture directories.
- [ ] Run a static-analysis rule (ESLint custom rule, or equivalent for the backend language) that flags any string-literal comparison against role names (`=== "owner"`, `=== "cashier"`) outside of the designated auth/RBAC middleware module — legitimate role-checking code lives in ONE place (Prompt 03's shared auth package), everywhere else should be calling that shared permission-check function, never re-implementing a string comparison.
- [ ] Secrets-scanning tool (gitleaks, per Prompt 03 Section 7) run against the FULL git history, not just the current commit, specifically hunting for any credential ever committed even if later removed.
- [ ] Database-vs-code cross-reference: for every dropdown/select list found in the frontend (Prompts 08-11's page specs), confirm a corresponding database table or settings-driven source exists — flag any dropdown whose options can only be found in frontend source code with no backing table.

